00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.830
Film Courage: The question is what's required to sell
your script in the current marketplace?

00:00:03.830 --> 00:00:08.639
The last time we visited with you Cory you
talked to us about this 'six script

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:13.559
cycles' and having pitch-perfect
authentic scripts. Have things changed?

00:00:13.559 --> 00:00:18.810
Corey Mandell, Instructor/Screenwriter: Things have just gotten better and to
really put things in perspective I

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:23.850
started teaching right during the
writers strike to 2007 and especially

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:28.680
after the writers strike it was bleak
there were writers with impressive

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.700
credits who couldn't get work it was
nearly impossible to sell a script all

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.649
the TV was almost all reality TV there
was very little scripted Studios were

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:42.329
all finalizing their consolidation and
they just weren't making movies back

00:00:42.329 --> 00:00:46.829
then it was like if a good month was one
or two of my students selling a pitch or

00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:51.750
an original script that was a good month
in the last week I've had 21 students

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:56.579
all pitches or pilot scripts that's a
pretty normal week so to put this in

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:02.850
perspective around 2002 HBO their entire
budget all-in for original content was

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:08.670
about five hundred five hundred million
dollars which is a lot of money this

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:13.430
year Netflix will be spending about
fifteen to sixteen billion dollars

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:17.580
amazon's about six billion dollars those
just netflix and amazon are spending

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:21.509
twenty one twenty two billion dollars
and everyone else is trying to catch up

00:01:21.509 --> 00:01:25.770
to them there's never been so much
content sold there's never been such an

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:32.189
insatiable demand for original material
now that said while it's far easier to

00:01:32.189 --> 00:01:37.229
sell a script than it used to it's still
not easy it's never easy to sell an

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:40.229
original script especially for an
unknown writer who doesn't have a track

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:44.549
record it's easier but it's not
necessarily easy but there are things

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:47.970
that people can do to give themselves a
